## Design Requirements

### What must change (the problems to fix)

**Problem 1 — Outdated card design:**
Current cards use an old card style inconsistent with WickUI. Cards must use the WickUI `Card` component with correct border radius, shadow token (`shadow-sm`), background token (`surface-default`), and padding tokens. Card titles must use the WickUI `heading-sm` typography token — not a custom font weight or size. Metric values must use `display-md` or `heading-xl` token. Supporting labels must use `body-sm` with `text-secondary` color token.

**Problem 2 — Gray box container not in design system:**
The large gray rounded container wrapping the three top cards and the Status Summary card is not a WickUI component. Remove it entirely. Cards sit directly on the page background (`bg-surface-page`) with standard page padding. No wrapper container, no extra border, no custom background box.

**Problem 3 — Outdated page layout:**
The current layout stacks cards awkwardly with uneven heights and inconsistent spacing. The new layout must use WickUI's standard grid system:
- Top row: 3 equal-width cards in a 3-column grid — Snapshot, Top Contributors, Top Goals
- Bottom section: Status Summary as a full-width card
- Consistent gap between all cards using the WickUI spacing token `gap-6`
- Page header ("Analytics") uses WickUI `page-title` typography token, left-aligned
- Time period dropdown and export button right-aligned in the page header row using flexbox space-between

### What must stay the same (functional parity)

- All 4 widgets must remain: Snapshot, Top Contributors, Top Goals, Status Summary
- All filters and toggles must remain functional
- Empty states must be preserved — "No Data" state with icon in Status Summary
- Export functionality must remain
- Top Goals donut chart with Percent/Count toggle and Status filter must remain
- Tasks / Initiatives tab toggle in Status Summary must remain

